| Module | Raw budget | Spatial / temporal job | Protected identity contribution | Failure if overdosed |
|---|---:|---|---|---|
| 1. Sparkling aperture | 580 uL | Thin, bright exterior shell at 0-5 min | Bergamot-citron and pale pepper announce L'Homme | Cologne sharpness or rough black-pepper bite |
| 2. Dual-state ginger prism | 640 uL | Cold wet-cut ginger at the surface; warm fibrous rhizome immediately behind it | Main recognizer and the bridge into the heart | Culinary ginger oil, lemon cleaner, or cardamom-led LNDL drift |
| 3. Violet-basil silk | 700 uL | Green leaf face over violet-woody fabric, with a small basil-flower seam | The characteristic L'Homme heart | Powdery iris, rose, or generic muguet |
| 4. Air and ozone field | 550 uL | Negative space around the heart; separates planes and projects the ginger-violet exchange | Modern daylight transparency | Blue aquatic, melon, metallic chemical glare |
| 5. Cedar-vetiver fiber | 1,530 uL | Natural grain, abstract halo, dry architecture, clean-earth/root shadow, and warm cedar depth | Tailored masculine base | Pencil-shaving monolith, harsh superamber, muddy naturals |
| 6. Tonka-sandal interior | 950 uL | A soft inner chamber behind the dry wood; fresh, creamy, and mineral sandalwood at different depths | Luxury warmth without changing family | Dessert sweetness or generic creamy sandalwood block |
| 7. Pressure/mineral contour | 330 uL | Gives edges, compression, and a cool-to-warm perimeter around the wood | Makes the base feel carved rather than flat | Scratchy amberwood or metallic overprojection |
| 8. Quiet adhesion matrix | 370 uL | Transparent film and slow mass that connect volatile and persistent layers | Smooth transitions and tactile polish | Oily heaviness or cosmetic salicylate character |
