### Three-dimensional transition map

| Window | Front plane | Middle plane | Rear plane | Required handoff |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0-5 min | Bergamot, cedrat, aldehydic peel, wet ginger | Linalyl/linalool body and pale pepper | First violet-leaf and cedar glints | Citrus must expose ginger rather than cover it |
| 15-45 min | Ginger/terpinyl freshness recedes | Parmavert-ionone-basil silk expands | Hedione HC, cyclamen, jasmine-body materials create air behind the leaf | Ginger must become fibrous and floral-green, not disappear abruptly |
| 1-3 h | Violet-green residue and dry spice | Diffusive cedar, vetiver, fresh sandalwood | Tonka, creamy sandalwood, mineral amber pressure | Heart must enter the wood through shared green, floral, and fibrous edges |
| 4-8 h+ | Dry cedar-vetiver grain | Tonka-sandal yielding interior | Warm cedar-amber shadow and clean woody musk veil | Base must retain differentiated grain, interior warmth, and outward air |

