## Final Selection, Rejection, and Survival Logic

The current build deliberately uses one exact musk. Romandolide was selected over Ethylene Brassylate because L'Homme needs outward clean-woody diffusion rather than a lactonic-creamy thickening; over Habanolide because warmth already exists in the sandalwood, tonka, Cashmeran, and Azarbre planes; and over Zenolide because a colder citrus musk could flatten the wet-to-warm ginger transition. Galaxolide, Tonalide, Macrolide, and Musk Ketone remain excluded as detergent, redundant, too quiet, or powder-genre shifting.

The four sandalwood materials survive provisionally because they occupy different modeled planes: Sandalore is the perceptible fresh face (OAV 7.0), Ebanol the more volatile creamy bridge (321), Polysantol the slow yielding interior (247), and Javanol the low-mass dry-mineral line (313). This is a design hypothesis, not proof that a nose will resolve four sandalwood layers; the blind read must prune any collapsed redundancy.

Cedarwood EO, Himalayan Cedarwood EO, Iso E Super, Timberol, Azarbre, Koavone, Vetikon, Vetival, and Indian vetiver form a wood topology rather than a list: literal grain, slow cedar shadow, molecular halo, dry edge, warm depth, internal bridge, green diffusion, suede fiber, and root respectively. Clearwood was tested computationally, modeled at OAV 0.06 for a role that required perceptibility, and was removed; its 100 uL was rebased into Cedarwood EO (+40), Himalayan Cedarwood (+30), and Vetiver (+30).

Verdox was considered but rejected: its fruity-green apple/woody character would pull the heart toward an apple facet when Parmavert, ionones, Cyclamen, and Scentenal already provide the target-linked violet-leaf architecture. Verdyl acetate is not live-inventory authority and is not needed in the ideal. Bontoux Cinnamon Oil is physically reported present, but the earlier favorable 10%/3 mL observation is formulation-specific; cinnamon would turn this daylight ginger-violet L'Homme toward La Nuit, amber-spice, or gourmand territory, so availability is not a reason to use it. Lemonile remains strictly the existing 1% DPG stock, never neat.

